WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.788
This guided practice is about policy not just syntax
Run the two

00:00:04.812 --> 00:00:09.875
status filters from the earlier slide and compare
the results Ordinary not-equal

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:14.950
excludes the NULL status because the comparison
becomes UNKNOWN IS DISTINCT FROM

00:00:14.962 --> 00:00:18.688
returns true for NULL compared with Paid so the
missing-status record is

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:24.275
included The additional row is Susan Gray's billing
record where payment_status

00:00:24.288 --> 00:00:29.712
is NULL Now explain the business meaning The first
query means known

00:00:29.738 --> 00:00:33.888
status and not Paid The second query means anything
that is not

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:38.700
definitely Paid including a missing status that may
need review Both can

00:00:38.712 --> 00:00:42.750
be valid The important skill is choosing the one
that matches the

00:00:42.762 --> 00:00:43.662
intended rule
